00:05:07.310 --> 00:05:11.930
Whether these venues are available and for which contracts depends on where you live,

00:05:12.470 --> 00:05:16.530
the rules differ by country, province and state, and they are changing.

00:05:17.563 --> 00:05:22.743
Who posts a quote and why a venue would pay for one is the mechanism in how it works today.

00:05:23.303 --> 00:05:28.503
A prediction market contract pays one of two amounts when it resolves, so size still open

00:05:28.503 --> 00:05:33.943
at the end jumps to a full payout or to zero. That settlement exposure is a different control

00:05:33.943 --> 00:05:39.183
problem from quoting a stock or a future you can roll. The number on the screen is a probability,

00:05:39.843 --> 00:05:43.783
and the quote is what turns an incoming order into an update of that probability.

00:05:44.343 --> 00:05:50.123
A paper on archive, optimal market making in prediction markets, models that price as a conditional

00:05:50.123 --> 00:05:55.983
probability generated by transforming a latent belief that defuses over time. The market maker

00:05:55.983 --> 00:05:59.663
picks a bid and an ask to maximize expected wealth at the end.

00:06:00.123 --> 00:06:04.983
Marked to market inventory risk while the market is open, and settlement risk on contracts

00:06:04.983 --> 00:06:08.063
left open at resolution, sit in the same problem.

00:06:08.583 --> 00:06:13.683
The authors derive the Hamilton-Jacobie Bellman equation, and characterize a unique optimal

00:06:13.683 --> 00:06:15.723
bid and a unique optimal ask.

00:06:16.183 --> 00:06:21.063
Shifting the equation into latent belief space and using a fixed point argument, they prove

00:06:21.063 --> 00:06:25.883
a classical solution exists and is unique, and they verify that the quoting rule from

00:06:25.883 --> 00:06:31.063
is optimal. Their comparison has no dollar figures in the abstract. A myopic

00:06:31.063 --> 00:06:36.183
quota maximizes only the instantaneous expected mark-to-market profit. The edge

00:06:36.183 --> 00:06:40.583
on the next trade marked at the new probability. The optimal rule also has to

00:06:40.583 --> 00:06:44.763
care how inventory behaves if the latent belief keeps moving and how that

00:06:44.763 --> 00:06:49.583
inventory pays if the event resolves either way. Inventory shifts the quote because

00:06:49.583 --> 00:06:53.883
a maker already longed the yes side is less willing to buy more of it and more

00:06:53.883 --> 00:06:58.623
willing to sell it. Market beliefs shift the quote because the latent probability is the thing

00:06:58.623 --> 00:07:03.443
being marked. Time to resolution shifts the quote because settlement risk dominates when the

00:07:03.443 --> 00:07:08.983
binary payoff is close, and marked to market risk has longer to compound when resolution is far.

00:07:09.703 --> 00:07:14.983
Risk aversion changes how hard those penalties bite, so a more risk averse maker posts a wider

00:07:14.983 --> 00:07:21.683
quote, or a sharper inventory skew for the same book. Against that myopic benchmark, the paper finds

00:07:21.683 --> 00:07:27.063
the optimal strategy substantially improves downside protection while preserving most expected

00:07:27.063 --> 00:07:32.723
profit. That is about how a quote is chosen once a liquidity setting exists, not a claim

00:07:32.723 --> 00:07:38.343
that one side of a live contract is cheap. The numerical analysis names dependence on inventory,

00:07:38.783 --> 00:07:44.423
beliefs, time to resolution, and risk aversion, and it does not report a live exchange test

00:07:44.423 --> 00:07:50.343
or a fee schedule. A second archive paper, adaptive liquidity in prediction markets via online

00:07:50.343 --> 00:07:54.223
and learning, asks how much liquidity the mechanism itself supplies.

00:07:54.803 --> 00:08:00.003
Markets need liquidity to turn trades into informative prices, and ordinary cost-function

00:08:00.003 --> 00:08:02.583
designs fix that liquidity before trading starts.

00:08:03.243 --> 00:08:08.523
The freeze locks a trade-off between price responsiveness and worst-case loss, even though order

00:08:08.523 --> 00:08:09.783
flow is not stationary.

00:08:10.383 --> 00:08:15.343
A thick book means one trade barely moves the probability, so the price looks calm for

00:08:15.343 --> 00:08:16.383
a mechanical reason.

00:08:16.383 --> 00:08:21.563
A thin setting means one trade swings it, and the mechanism's worst-case loss is the

00:08:21.563 --> 00:08:23.383
other side of that same design choice.

00:08:23.983 --> 00:08:28.283
Their construction mixes a family of cost-function markets with weights that can be learned,

00:08:28.743 --> 00:08:30.303
and the mix is still one market.

00:08:30.863 --> 00:08:36.403
The abstract says it preserves no arbitrage, a bounded worst-case loss, expressiveness, and

00:08:36.403 --> 00:08:37.403
a positive upside.

00:08:37.963 --> 00:08:42.923
Each round, a hybrid structural risk signal scores price impact against inventory risk.

00:08:42.923 --> 00:08:47.823
Standard online learning algorithms then get switching regret guarantees against the best

00:08:47.823 --> 00:08:52.703
sequence of liquidity regimes in hindsight, not merely the single best fixed regime.

00:08:53.243 --> 00:08:57.723
Simulations show the weight shifting when order flow changes and when inventory changes.

00:08:58.223 --> 00:09:02.883
Neither paper names a venue reward schedule or a dollar subsidy paid to quotas.

00:09:03.283 --> 00:09:08.063
What they do establish is why a quote has to be paid for in the spread or in some other

00:09:08.063 --> 00:09:13.203
compensation. With nobody posting a bid and an ask, a trade has nowhere to land, and

00:09:13.203 --> 00:09:14.783
the probability does not update.

00:09:15.463 --> 00:09:20.603
Liquidity set too high dolls that update. Liquidity set too low lets one order rewrite

00:09:20.603 --> 00:09:25.723
the probability and raises worst case loss. A tight spread is a quote someone was willing

00:09:25.723 --> 00:09:31.843
or compensated to post. Not a second independent vote that the probability is right. Volume that

00:09:31.843 --> 00:09:36.883
is a maker trading against incoming orders is flow through a quote, not a pile of separate

00:09:36.883 --> 00:09:42.423
forecasts. A price near resolution is not the same object as a price months out, because

00:09:42.423 --> 00:09:47.483
one paper puts time inside the quoting decision, and the other lets the liquidity regime switch

00:09:47.483 --> 00:09:53.229
as conditions change. Neither result tells you which side of a contract to take. Before

00:09:53.229 --> 00:09:58.989
we go, AgCon meets Thursday and Friday in Overland Park, with the CFTC and Kansas State

